<!-- ItemCookingDef.xml Documentation

	- This file helps power the cooking formula in Open RSC.

	- <int> values represent the ID of the raw version of that food.

	- low and high values help decide burn chance, and are either from RSCSundae (F2P items) or OSRS wiki (P2P items).
	  - <low> and <high> are the default chances to burn, and always apply to normal ranges
		- <lowFire> and <highFire> are the chances to burn at campfires or fireplaces
		- <lowCooksRange> and <highCooksRange> are the chances to burn at a cook's range (e.g. Lumbridge range)
		- <lowGauntlets> and <highGauntlets> are the chances to burn with gauntlets on (regardless of what you're cooking on)
		- If one of the non-default low/high values are not present, they fall back to the default ones.
		- Normal ranges were picked as the default low/high because you can always cook something on a range. Not true for campfires.
	  
	- For custom RSC foods, and foods for which low/high values could not be determined,
		low/high rates are omitted and the old formula is used.
-->
